#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Per-CPU detection of speculative execution vulnerabilities, kernel parameters Ditana applies by default, and how to verify or override them after installation."
msgstr "Identificaziun per mintga CPU da las mancanzas da segirezza da l’execuziun speculativa, ils parameters dal kernel che Ditana applitgescha sco standard, e co verifitgar u remplazzar quels suenter l’installaziun."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "CPU vulnerability mitigations"
msgstr "Mitigiaziuns da mancanzas da segirezza da la CPU"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Ditana enables CPU vulnerability mitigations in **High Security mode** by default. The installer detects which mitigations your specific CPU needs by reading `/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/`, then offers each as an individually-toggleable checkbox in the **Expert Settings → CPU Vulnerability Mitigation Options** dialog. This page documents every option in detail."
msgstr "Ditana activescha sco standard las mitigiaziuns da mancanzas da segirezza da la CPU en il **High Security mode**. L’installatur identifitgescha tge mitigiaziuns che Vossa CPU specifica dovra, cun leger `/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/`, e porscha lura mintgina sco chaschetta da controlla che sa lascha activar e deactivar individualmain en il dialog **Expert Settings → CPU Vulnerability Mitigation Options**. Questa pagina documentescha detagliadamain mintga opziun."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default kernel settings vs Ditana's mitigations"
msgstr "Parameters da standard dal kernel cunter las mitigiaziuns da Ditana"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "The upstream Linux defaults balance security against performance and leave certain vulnerabilities unmitigated unless explicitly opted in. Ditana opts in by default — for most workloads the cost is negligible, while the security benefit is substantial. You can revert any individual mitigation in the installer if you have a workload that demonstrably benefits."
msgstr "Las valurs da standard dal Linux d’origin tschertgan in equiliber tranter segirezza e prestaziun e laschan tschertas mancanzas da segirezza senza mitigiaziun, sch’ins n’activescha betg explicitamain la mitigiaziun. Ditana activescha las mitigiaziuns sco standard – per la gronda part da las chargias da lavur è il cust negligibel, entant ch’il profit per la segirezza è considerabel. Vus pudais deactivar en l’installatur mintga mitigiaziun individuala, sche Vus avais ina chargia da lavur che profitescha cumprovadamain da quai."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "The mitigation logic is hardware-specific. Only the vulnerabilities your CPU actually exhibits are configured; everything else is left at the kernel default."
msgstr "La logica da las mitigiaziuns è specifica per la hardware. Mo las mancanzas da segirezza che Vossa CPU ha effectivamain vegnan configuradas; tut il rest resta tar la valur da standard dal kernel."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "After installation"
msgstr "Suenter l’installaziun"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Several mitigations involve disabling Simultaneous Multi-Threading (SMT, also known as Hyper-Threading) as a fallback. Ditana's [custom terminal header](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-print-system-infos) shows which mitigations are active and whether SMT is on or off."
msgstr "Pliras mitigiaziuns cumpiglian la deactivaziun dal Simultaneous Multi-Threading (SMT, er enconuschent sco Hyper-Threading) sco soluziun da reserva. Il [chau-pagina persunalisà dal terminal](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-print-system-infos) da Ditana mussa tge mitigiaziuns ch’èn activas e sche SMT è activà u deactivà."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "You can also verify with:"
msgstr "Vus pudais er verifitgar cun:"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "lscpu\n"
msgstr "lscpu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "To compare performance with and without a specific mitigation, edit the kernel command line for a single boot and remove the parameter associated with the mitigation you want to test. On a ZFS installation, which is what the Standard profile produces, that is accomplished via the ZFSBootMenu boot-environment editor; on a system that boots through GRUB, press `e` at the menu. The parameters are listed below under \"Applied parameter\" for each entry. Reboot and run your real workload – synthetic benchmarks rarely capture real impact."
msgstr "Per cumparegliar la prestaziun cun e senza ina tscherta mitigiaziun, modifitgai la lingia da cumond dal kernel per in sulet aviar ed allontanai il parameter che tutga tar la mitigiaziun che Vus vulais testar. En in’installaziun cun ZFS – quella ch’il profil Standard creescha – fa ins quai cun l’editur da boot environments da ZFSBootMenu; sin in sistem che vegn avià cun GRUB, squitschai `e` en il menu. Ils parameters èn enumerads sutvart per mintga endataziun sut «Parameter applitgà». Reaviai ed exequi Vossa vaira chargia da lavur – benchmarks sintetics mussan darar l’effect real."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "To make a change permanent on a ZFS installation, set the command line within the boot environment:"
msgstr "Per fixar permanentamain ina midada en in’installaziun cun ZFS, defini la lingia da cumond en il boot environment:"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo zfs set org.zfsbootmenu:commandline=\"rw <options>\" ditana-root/ROOT\n"
"zfs get org.zfsbootmenu:commandline ditana-root/ROOT\n"
msgstr ""
"sudo zfs set org.zfsbootmenu:commandline=\"rw <options>\" ditana-root/ROOT\n"
"zfs get org.zfsbootmenu:commandline ditana-root/ROOT\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "To make it permanent on a system that launches via GRUB, edit `/etc/default/grub`, find the `GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT` line (first save a backup), remove the parameter, then run:"
msgstr "Per fixar permanentamain la midada sin in sistem che vegn avià cun GRUB, modifitgai `/etc/default/grub`, tschertgai la lingia `GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT` (faschai l’emprim ina copia da segirezza), allontanai il parameter ed exequi lura:"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg\n"
msgstr "sudo grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "If a change prevents booting, edit the kernel command line in the GRUB menu to recover, then repeat the edit and `grub-mkconfig`."
msgstr "Sch’ina midada impedescha l’aviar, modifitgai la lingia da cumond dal kernel en il menu da GRUB per restaurar il sistem, e repeti lura la modificaziun e `grub-mkconfig`."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mitigations Ditana enables by default"
msgstr "Mitigiaziuns che Ditana activescha sco standard"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spectre variant 2 — Branch Target Injection"
msgstr "Spectre varianta 2 – Branch Target Injection"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Speculative execution exploit allowing attackers to read sensitive data via mistrained indirect branch predictors. Ditana applies the full mitigation (Indirect Branch Prediction Barrier always-on rather than conditional)."
msgstr "Attatga cun execuziun speculativa che permetta da leger datas sensiblas tras ina predicziun manipulada da sigls indirects. Ditana applitgescha la mitigiaziun cumpletta (Indirect Branch Prediction Barrier adina activa empè da cundiziunala)."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> All Spectre variant 2 mitigations can be forced on at boot time for all programs. This will add overhead as indirect branch speculations for all programs will be restricted.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: Spectre](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/spectre.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> Tut las mitigiaziuns da Spectre varianta 2 pon vegnir activadas obligatoricamain durant l’aviar per tut ils programs. Quai chaschuna custs supplementars, perquai che las speculaziuns da sigls indirects vegnan restrenschidas per tut ils programs.\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: Spectre](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/spectre.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Spectre v2` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Spectre Variant 2 Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `spectre_v2=on` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificatur `lscpu` | `Spectre v2` |\n"
"| Num dal parameter | *Enforce Spectre Variant 2 Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parameter applitgà | `spectre_v2=on` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "L1 Terminal Fault (L1TF)"
msgstr "L1 Terminal Fault (L1TF)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Affects Intel CPUs, allowing unauthorized access to data in the L1 cache. Ditana enforces full mitigation with aggressive cache flushing."
msgstr "Pertutga CPUs dad Intel e permetta in access betg autorisà a datas en il cache L1. Ditana sforza la mitigiaziun cumpletta cun svidar agressivamain il cache."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The kernel does not by default enforce the disabling of SMT, which leaves SMT systems vulnerable when running untrusted guests with EPT enabled.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: L1TF](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/l1tf.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> Il kernel na sforza betg sco standard la deactivaziun da SMT, uschia che sistems cun SMT restan pertutgads, cura ch’els exequeschan sistems giast betg fidads cun EPT activà.\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: L1TF](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/l1tf.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `L1tf` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce L1 Terminal Fault Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `l1tf=full,force` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificatur `lscpu` | `L1tf` |\n"
"| Num dal parameter | *Enforce L1 Terminal Fault Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parameter applitgà | `l1tf=full,force` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Microarchitectural Data Sampling (MDS)"
msgstr "Microarchitectural Data Sampling (MDS)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Allows attackers to sample data from CPU buffers. Full mitigation may disable SMT if necessary."
msgstr "Ina persuna ch’attatga il sistem po prender mustras da datas ord ils buffers da la CPU. La mitigiaziun cumpletta po deactivar SMT, sche necessari."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The kernel does not by default enforce the disabling of SMT, which leaves SMT systems vulnerable when running untrusted code.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: MDS](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/mds.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> Il kernel na sforza betg sco standard la deactivaziun da SMT, uschia che sistems cun SMT restan pertutgads, cura ch’els exequeschan code betg fidà.\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: MDS](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/mds.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Mds` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce MDS Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `mds=full,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificatur `lscpu` | `Mds` |\n"
"| Num dal parameter | *Enforce MDS Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parameter applitgà | `mds=full,nosmt` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "TSX Asynchronous Abort (TAA)"
msgstr "TSX Asynchronous Abort (TAA)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Affects CPUs with Transactional Synchronization Extensions. Full mitigation may disable SMT if required."
msgstr "Pertutga CPUs cun Transactional Synchronization Extensions. La mitigiaziun cumpletta po deactivar SMT, sche necessari."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> TSX might be disabled if microcode provides a TSX control MSR. If so, system is not vulnerable.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: TAA](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/tsx_async_abort.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> TSX po vegnir deactivà, sch’il microcode porscha in MSR da controlla per TSX. En quest cas n’è il sistem betg pertutgà.\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: TAA](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/tsx_async_abort.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Tsx async abort` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce TSX Async Abort Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `tsx_async_abort=full,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificatur `lscpu` | `Tsx async abort` |\n"
"| Num dal parameter | *Enforce TSX Async Abort Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parameter applitgà | `tsx_async_abort=full,nosmt` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Meltdown (L1D flushing)"
msgstr "Meltdown (svidar il cache L1D)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Speculative execution exploit allowing kernel memory reads from userspace. Ditana forces L1 data cache flushing."
msgstr "Attatga cun execuziun speculativa che permetta da leger la memoria dal kernel a partir dal spazi d’utilisader. Ditana sforza il svidar dal cache da datas L1."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The kernel command line allows to control the L1D flush mitigations at boot time with the option `l1d_flush=`. By default the mechanism is disabled.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: L1D flush](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/l1d_flush.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> La lingia da cumond dal kernel permetta da reglar durant l’aviar las mitigiaziuns tras svidar il cache L1D cun l’opziun `l1d_flush=`. Sco standard è il mecanissem deactivà.\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: L1D flush](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/l1d_flush.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Meltdown` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Meltdown Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `l1d_flush=on` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificatur `lscpu` | `Meltdown` |\n"
"| Num dal parameter | *Enforce Meltdown Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parameter applitgà | `l1d_flush=on` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "MMIO Stale Data"
msgstr "MMIO Stale Data"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Data leakage from memory-mapped I/O. Full mitigation may disable SMT."
msgstr "Fugia da datas dal memory-mapped I/O. La mitigiaziun cumpletta po deactivar SMT."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> `full,nosmt` — Same as `full`, with SMT disabled on vulnerable CPUs. This is the complete mitigation.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: MMIO stale data](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/processor_mmio_stale_data.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> `full,nosmt` – Il medem sco `full`, cun SMT deactivà sin CPUs pertutgadas. Quai è la mitigiaziun cumpletta.\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: MMIO stale data](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/processor_mmio_stale_data.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Mmio stale data` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce MMIO Stale Data Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `mmio_stale_data=full,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificatur `lscpu` | `Mmio stale data` |\n"
"| Num dal parameter | *Enforce MMIO Stale Data Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parameter applitgà | `mmio_stale_data=full,nosmt` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retbleed — Cross-Thread Return Address Predictions"
msgstr "Retbleed – Cross-Thread Return Address Predictions"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Speculative execution attack leaking return addresses. Auto-selected mitigation may disable SMT."
msgstr "Attatga cun execuziun speculativa che tradescha adressas da return. La mitigiaziun tschernida automaticamain po deactivar SMT."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> `auto,nosmt` — automatically select a mitigation, disabling SMT if necessary for the full mitigation.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: kernel parameters](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> `auto,nosmt` – tscherner automaticamain ina mitigiaziun e deactivar SMT, sche quai è necessari per la mitigiaziun cumpletta.\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: kernel parameters](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Retbleed` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Retbleed Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `retbleed=auto,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificatur `lscpu` | `Retbleed` |\n"
"| Num dal parameter | *Enforce Retbleed Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parameter applitgà | `retbleed=auto,nosmt` |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "See also [kernel.org: Cross-Thread Return Address Predictions](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/cross-thread-rsb.html)."
msgstr "Guardai er [kernel.org: Cross-Thread Return Address Predictions](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/cross-thread-rsb.html)."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Speculative Return Stack Overflow (SRSO)"
msgstr "Speculative Return Stack Overflow (SRSO)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Speculative attacks via the return stack buffer. Combines IBPB barriers with strict spectre_v2-user mode."
msgstr "Attatgas speculativas via il return stack buffer. Cumbinescha barrieras IBPB cun il modus strict spectre_v2-user."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> `Mitigation: IBPB`: Similar protection as \"safe RET\" but employs an IBPB barrier on privilege domain crossings (User→Kernel, Guest→Host).\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: SRSO](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/srso.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> `Mitigation: IBPB`: Protecziun sumeglianta a «safe RET», ma cun ina barriera IBPB tar ils passadis tranter domenas da privilegis (User→Kernel, Guest→Host).\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: SRSO](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/srso.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Spec rstack overflow` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce SRSO Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `spec_rstack_overflow=ibpb spectre_v2_user=on` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificatur `lscpu` | `Spec rstack overflow` |\n"
"| Num dal parameter | *Enforce SRSO Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parameter applitgà | `spec_rstack_overflow=ibpb spectre_v2_user=on` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gather Data Sampling (GDS)"
msgstr "Gather Data Sampling (GDS)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Affects AVX instructions. Forces microcode mitigation, or disables AVX where microcode is unavailable."
msgstr "Pertutga las instrucziuns AVX. Sforza la mitigiaziun tras microcode u deactivescha AVX, nua che microcode n’è betg disponibel."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Specifying `gather_data_sampling=force` will use the microcode mitigation when available or disable AVX on affected systems where the microcode hasn't been updated to include the mitigation.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: Gather Data Sampling](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/gather_data_sampling.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> Cun `gather_data_sampling=force` vegn utilisada la mitigiaziun tras microcode, sch’ella è disponibla, u AVX vegn deactivà sin sistems pertutgads, nua ch’il microcode n’è betg vegnì actualisà per cuntegnair la mitigiaziun.\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: Gather Data Sampling](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/gather_data_sampling.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Gather data sampling` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Gather Data Sampling Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `gather_data_sampling=force` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificatur `lscpu` | `Gather data sampling` |\n"
"| Num dal parameter | *Enforce Gather Data Sampling Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parameter applitgà | `gather_data_sampling=force` |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Register File Data Sampling (RFDS)"
msgstr "Register File Data Sampling (RFDS)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Allows sampling of data from CPU registers."
msgstr "Permetta da prender mustras da datas ord ils registers da la CPU."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> This parameter overrides the compile time default set by `CONFIG_MITIGATION_RFDS`.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: kernel parameters](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> Quest parameter remplazza la valur da standard fixada durant la cumpilaziun tras `CONFIG_MITIGATION_RFDS`.\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: kernel parameters](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Reg file data sampling` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce RFDS Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `reg_file_data_sampling=on` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| Identificatur `lscpu` | `Reg file data sampling` |\n"
"| Num dal parameter | *Enforce RFDS Mitigation* |\n"
"| Parameter applitgà | `reg_file_data_sampling=on` |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "See also [kernel.org: RFDS](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/reg-file-data-sampling.html)."
msgstr "Guardai er [kernel.org: RFDS](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/reg-file-data-sampling.html)."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vulnerabilities not exposed in the installer"
msgstr "Mancanzas da segirezza che l’installatur na mussa betg"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "The kernel performs maximum mitigation by default for these — there is nothing for Ditana to add."
msgstr "Per quellas applitgescha il kernel sco standard la mitigiaziun maximala – Ditana n’ha nagut d’agiuntar."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Five more are reported by the kernel and named nowhere above, because Ditana adds nothing to them either: Ghostwrite, Indirect Target Selection, old microcode, TSA and VMSCAPE. The kernel decides what each of them needs from the processor it finds and leaves the result where `lscpu` and `/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/` show it."
msgstr "Il kernel annunzia anc tschintg ulteriuras che na vegnan numnadas nagliur survart, perquai che Ditana n’agiuntescha er a quellas nagut: Ghostwrite, Indirect Target Selection, old microcode, TSA e VMSCAPE. Il kernel decida tenor il processur ch’el chatta tge che mintgina da quellas dovra, e lascha il resultat là, nua che `lscpu` e `/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/` mussan quel."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spectre variant 1 — Bounds Check Bypass"
msgstr "Spectre varianta 1 – Bounds Check Bypass"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> There is no guarantee that all possible attack vectors for Spectre variant 1 are covered.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: Spectre](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/spectre.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> I na dat nagina garanzia che tut ils vecturs d’attatga pussaivels per Spectre varianta 1 sajan cuverts.\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: Spectre](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/spectre.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "`lscpu` identifier: `Spectre v1`"
msgstr "Identificatur `lscpu`: `Spectre v1`"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "iTLB multihit"
msgstr "iTLB multihit"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "`lscpu` identifier: `Itlb multihit`. See [kernel.org: iTLB multihit](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/multihit.html)."
msgstr "Identificatur `lscpu`: `Itlb multihit`. Guardai [kernel.org: iTLB multihit](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/multihit.html)."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "SRBDS — Special Register Buffer Data Sampling"
msgstr "SRBDS – Special Register Buffer Data Sampling"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "`lscpu` identifier: `Srbds`. See [kernel.org: SRBDS](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/special-register-buffer-data-sampling.html)."
msgstr "Identificatur `lscpu`: `Srbds`. Guardai [kernel.org: SRBDS](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/special-register-buffer-data-sampling.html)."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Speculative Store Bypass (SSB)"
msgstr "Speculative Store Bypass (SSB)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The kernel provides mitigation for such vulnerabilities in various forms.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: spec_ctrl](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/userspace-api/spec_ctrl.html)\n"
msgstr ""
"> Il kernel porscha mitigiaziun per talas mancanzas da segirezza en differentas furmas.\n"
">\n"
"> – [kernel.org: spec_ctrl](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/userspace-api/spec_ctrl.html)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "`lscpu` identifier: `Spec store bypass`."
msgstr "Identificatur `lscpu`: `Spec store bypass`."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mitigation reduction — at your own risk"
msgstr "Reducziun da las mitigiaziuns – a Voss agen ristg"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "The installer also exposes two options that *reduce* mitigations. These significantly increase your exposure to known CPU vulnerabilities. Use only with a clear, justified reason."
msgstr "L’installatur porscha er duas opziuns che *reduceschan* las mitigiaziuns. Quellas augmentan considerablamain Vossa exposiziun a mancanzas da segirezza enconuschentas da la CPU. Utilisai quellas mo cun in motiv cler e giustifitgà."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disable Intel Indirect Branch Tracking — `ibt=off`"
msgstr "Deactivar Intel Indirect Branch Tracking – `ibt=off`"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Turns off the kernel's Indirect Branch Tracking. IBT is the forward-edge half of Control-flow Enforcement Technology – the hardware checks that every indirect jump or call lands on an `endbr` instruction, which is what makes jump-oriented and call-oriented programming hard. It is control-flow integrity, not a speculative-execution mitigation: Branch Target Injection is Spectre v2, elaborated upon earlier under `spectre_v2=on`. This kernel parameter is **undocumented** in the official kernel parameters reference, even though it is commonly enabled by default on certain distributions without any explicit communication."
msgstr "Deactivescha l’Indirect Branch Tracking dal kernel. IBT è la mesadad forward-edge da la Control-flow Enforcement Technology – la hardware controllescha che mintga sigl u appel indirect arriva sin in’instrucziun `endbr`, e quai renda difficila la programmaziun orientada a sigls ed ad appels. I sa tracta da l’integritad dal fluss da controlla, betg d’ina mitigiaziun da l’execuziun speculativa: Branch Target Injection è Spectre v2, explitgà pli baud sut `spectre_v2=on`. Quest parameter dal kernel **n’è betg documentà** en la referenza uffiziala dals parameters dal kernel, schebain ch’el è savens activà sco standard en tschertas distribuziuns senza nagina communicaziun explicita."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "The kernel documents the other half of CET, the user-space shadow stack, at [shstk](https://docs.kernel.org/next/x86/shstk.html); IBT itself has no page of its own there."
msgstr "Il kernel documentescha l’autra mesadad da CET, il shadow stack en il spazi d’utilisader, sut [shstk](https://docs.kernel.org/next/x86/shstk.html); IBT sez n’ha là nagina atgna pagina."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disable all mitigations — `mitigations=off`"
msgstr "Deactivar tut las mitigiaziuns – `mitigations=off`"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "This is **stronger than unchecking every individual mitigation** in the dialog. With `mitigations=off`, the kernel skips *every* mitigation it knows about — including the ones Ditana doesn't expose because they're on by default. The performance ceiling rises; the security floor drops, hard."
msgstr "Quai è **pli ferm che deactivar mintga mitigiaziun singula** en il dialog. Cun `mitigations=off` sursiglia il kernel *mintga* mitigiaziun ch’el enconuscha – inclus quellas che Ditana na mussa betg, perquai ch’ellas èn activas sco standard. La limita superiura da la prestaziun crescha; il nivel minimal da la segirezza croda, e quai fermamain."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Only useful for benchmarks, air-gapped systems with full physical control, or environments where you have categorically other defences."
msgstr "Quai è util mo per benchmarks, per sistems isolads da mintga rait cun controlla fisica cumpletta u per ambients, en ils quals Vus avais mesiras da protecziun da tut in’autra categoria."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "See [kernel.org: kernel parameters](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)."
msgstr "Guardai [kernel.org: kernel parameters](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disclaimer"
msgstr "Exclusiun da responsabladad"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "The guidance here is based on the [official CPU vulnerability documentation](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/index.html) and the [kernel command-line parameter reference](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html). Different kernel branches occasionally diverge from these defaults in subtle ways; our testing covers the Ditana-supported kernels, but unusual hardware combinations can produce edge cases."
msgstr "Las indicaziuns qua sa basan sin la [documentaziun uffiziala davart las mancanzas da segirezza da la CPU](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/index.html) e sin la [referenza dals parameters da la lingia da cumond dal kernel](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html). Differents roms dal kernel divergeschan mintgatant da questas valurs da standard en moda subtila; noss tests cuvran ils kernels sustegnids da Ditana, ma cumbinaziuns da hardware nunusitadas pon chaschunar cas extrems."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "If you have a workload that benefits from a different default, or if you find a CPU model where Ditana's detection is incomplete or incorrect: please [open a GitHub issue](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-config/issues) or email support@ditana.org. The detection logic is data, not code — so improvements are usually a few KDL lines."
msgstr "Sche Vus avais ina chargia da lavur che profitescha d’in’autra valur da standard, u sche Vus chattais in model da CPU, per il qual l’identificaziun da Ditana è incumpletta u incorrecta: per plaschair [avri in issue sin GitHub](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-config/issues) u scrivai in e-mail a support@ditana.org. La logica d’identificaziun è datas, betg code – uschia èn meglieraziuns per regla in pèr lingias KDL."
